Momentors — "Attention : xyz"
=============================
    All cross momentors are announced as "Attention : <cross>":
        1PX / 5PX     (PVT zero-crosses)
        1M2X / 5M2X   (MACD2 signal crosses)
        VOC crosses   (once volume is in the export)
    Downswing: cross-DOWN momentors + VOC cross-UP moments (volume warning against the swing)
    Upswing: cross-UP momentors + VOC cross-DOWN moments
    // 15s PVT/MACD2 crosses are NOT announced separately — they only appear
    // inside the 1PXD_15PM / 1PXU_15PM confirmation.


Rules
=====
    1. Gap up/down in % at session open (only numeric value ever announced).
    2. Never mention Nifty price or level values — level NAMES only.
    3. D WAP has nothing to do with D PM. D PM is Daily PVT/MACD2; its trend
       decides whether 30m EMA50/100/200 act as support or resistance.
    4. "Expect 1PXU_15PM Swing Ups" only when 5m PVT has started uptrending
       (mirror: "Expect 1PXD_15PM Swing Down" only when 5m PVT downtrending).
    5. Stochastic zones only: OBZ / MZ / OSZ — no values. 5m timeframe only.
    6. Retests count only after price moved ~25 pts away and returned
       (3rd+ touch = "...again").
    7. VWAP proximity warning fires within ~10 pts, once per direction per episode.
    8. 15s PVT/MACD2 crosses are never announced standalone — they only confirm
       1PXD_15PM / 1PXU_15PM.
    9. Support/resistance touches are announced for ALL EMAs (1m/5m/30m —
       EXCLUDING EMA9: no 1E9 / 5E9), all Pivotal Levels and VWAP, as price
       travels up and down. Values of these EMAs/levels track their live bars.
       EMA names: 1E21/1E50/1E100/1E200, 5E21/5E50/5E100/5E200, 30m EMA50/100/200.
    8. 15s PVT/MACD2 crosses are never announced standalone — they only confirm
       1PXD_15PM / 1PXU_15PM.
   10. Same-tick touches are GROUPED into one line to keep it less noisy:
       "Price retested support 1E100 and 1E200 again".
   11. "5PX about to cross down/up": the 5m PVT is read ON THE 1M TIMEFRAME
       (developing value, updates every minute). "cross down" ONLY when that
       value is ABOVE zero but within +/-0.1 of the line, and 1m PVT<0 with
       1m MACD2 falling; "cross up" ONLY when it is BELOW zero within +/-0.1,
       and 1m PVT>0 with 1m MACD2 rising. Once per episode — re-arms after the
       5m PVT (1m view) moves outside the band or crosses the line.
